  "answer_text": "The maximum length of the IPsec Pre-Shared Key (PSK) for IPsec tunnels is up to 64 characters. When changing a site's Connection Type from IKEv1 to IKEv2, you may lose compatibility with devices that do not support IKEv2; some devices cannot use the same IKEv2 parameters, so IKEv1 may be required, and Azure policy-based VPN gateways, for example, only support IKEv1. In general, IKEv2 is recommended when available for better efficiency and reliability, but you may need to stay on IKEv1 for compatibility.",
